---
description: Rules for the Claude assistant (Phase 3) and anything sent to an AI
alwaysApply: false
---

# AI assistant

- The assistant uses the action registry as its tool list. It cannot do
  anything the panel buttons cannot do.
- Read tools (`server/src/assistant/chat.ts`) run directly and only read.
  Every registry action is a proposal tool: calling it only adds a card, and
  the card runs through `/api/actions/:id` when the user clicks Run.
- Actions that delete data or need the user's own typed confirmation or
  upload are in `ASSISTANT_EXCLUDED_ACTIONS` and never become tools.
- The assistant's own settings (enabled, model, key) are plain routes, never
  registry actions, so it cannot change them.
- Every tool result goes through `redact()` and is capped in size.
- The database overview tool (`databaseSummary` in
  `server/src/mysql-wordpress.ts`) gives table and option names, sizes and
  counts only: never a value from a row, a user, an email or an option value.
- Never send to the model: database contents, `wp-config.php` secrets (DB
  password, salts, keys), `secrets.json`, private keys, full log files. Log
  excerpts are short and redacted.
- Each teammate uses their own Anthropic API key or `ant auth login`; it is
  stored outside the repo, readable only by them.
- The assistant is optional and off by default; every page must work without
  it.
- The MCP server (`server/src/mcp.ts`, `devmagic-panel mcp`) exposes the same
  read tools and the same proposals as `propose_*` tools. Proposals go to the
  `proposals` table and run only from the panel; MCP clients can run with
  their own approvals switched off, so they never get a tool that changes the
  system.
- Installing from an organization runs Claude Code headless
  (`server/src/org/claude-code.ts`) with the user's own claude.ai sign-in and
  connectors. Every run gets a fixed list of read-only tools (file reads in
  its own folder, Asana reads, Drive metadata and search, Docs reads; never
  Drive file contents), `--disallowedTools` for anything that writes or runs
  commands, a model, an effort (`--effort`) and a spending cap, and a JSON
  schema; the answer is checked again with zod (`shared/src/org.ts`: links,
  Drive ids, dump names) before use. Reading a repo and checking its links
  are the registry actions `org.readRepo` and `org.checkAccess`
  (`changesSystem: false`, kept from the assistant): jobs that note
  themselves on the install draft with what they are for, and keep their
  answer there (`Drafts.noteJob`, `saveResult`).
- A repo is read from a folder holding only its doc and build files
  (`docPaths`), never `wp-config.php` or `.env`. Dumps are downloaded by the
  panel with rclone or taken from Downloads; their contents never reach
  Claude.
- The wizard's answers from an organization follow the local setup first
  (`prefillFromFacts`): local.* names, wpcore, the cores installed here.
  Where the docs differ it says so; what nothing answers stays empty.
